ification/indeterminate return, not just the 4 sev-variable sites); and needs to confirm whether completion_verdict.schema.json truly shares common.schema.json's $defs/finding with review_result.schema.json (if so, relaxing the shared required list technically loosens both, though completion-verification's own producers always populate severity in practice regardless of the schema requirement). Dispatched research on normalize_finding's full caller set (to see if changing it to leave severity absent-when-absent, rather than backfilling \"info\", would break anything) before rewriting ticket 6 a second time.","timestamp":1788147285415956003},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ticket 6 (byzantine-spinelike-penguin, FINAL ticket) plan-review PASSED on 2nd attempt after fixing the critical normalize_finding re-stamp gap the gate caught: added a 3rd fix layer (findings.py::normalize_finding only clamps to \"info\" when severity is present-but-invalid, never backfills when the key is genuinely absent -- confirmed safe against every production caller and existing test via dedicated research), fixed decide.py's 5th severity-stamping site (hardcoded \"none\" literal on the no-verification path, not just the 4 sev-variable sites), and added findings.py + its test file to file_impact (missing from the original scope). Claiming ticket 6 now -- this is the last ticket; once it closes, the epic itself closes and Phase 6 (land the whole stack) begins.","timestamp":1788147935745805781},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ticket 6 TDD held-out loop: wrote 3 new RED tests (decide.py no-severity, normalize_finding absent-stays-absent, shim.py present-value-passthrough) plus fixed 3 now-stale existing assertions (test_divergence_grade_split.py x2, test_plan_review.py x1 -- these asserted pass3_decide's output carried severity, which is deliberately being retired; fixed under revert-first discipline) and replaced 1 obsolete parametrized test (test_shim_maps_kernel_severity_to_common_vocabulary, which tested the _KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY map being deleted) with 2 new tests. Held out the full-chain integration test (shim -> finalize_findings -> normalize_finding -> final review_result has no severity key) -- the exact composition defect the plan-review gate caught -- physically removed from test_code_review_ws4.py, saved to /Users/joeoakhart/.claude/jobs/f3367052/tmp/heldout/test_code_review_ws4_FULL.py. Made the schema relaxation edit myself (common.schema.json: severity removed from finding.required, property/enum kept). Dispatched implementer subagent for decide.py, shim.py, findings.py, config.py cleanup (SEVERITIES/DEFAULT_BLOCKING_SEVERITIES/blocking_severities/_severities_env removal), and the two review_bot test file updates. Now drafting the ADR amendment + release-notes/CHANGELOG compatibility-note entries myself (docs work).","timestamp":1788148301721844369},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ticket 6 full-suite validation: 18318 passed, 13 failed, 63 skipped in 2:08:16 -- identical failure set to the earlier ticket-2 run (9x ruff-not-on-PATH environmental, 1x stale generated types.py), confirming zero regressions from this large change. Also confirmed via Gerrit REST: tickets 1-5's changes (2441,2445,2447,2452,2453) are all MERGED on origin/main -- the human operator (Joe Oakhart, via admin identity) submitted 2445/2447/2452/2453 manually as they went green, ahead of the epic's planned Phase-6 batch land; ticket 1 was submitted by me via the early-land exception. Proceeding to commit and push ticket 6.","timestamp":1788156580502535181},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ticket 6 (byzantine-spinelike-penguin, FINAL ticket) implemented: pass3_decide stops stamping severity at all 5 return sites; shim.py passes through explicit severity unchanged, omits when absent (deleted _KERNEL_TO_COMMON_SEVERITY/_SEVERITY_DEFAULT); normalize_finding only clamps present-but-invalid values, never backfills absent ones; common.schema.json relaxes severity to optional; removed vestigial BLOCKING_SEVERITIES/SEVERITIES/_severities_env from review_bot/config.py + updated its 2 tests; fixed a docs-drift gate (gen_env_registry.py/env-vars.md) the implementer caught; wrote release-notes.md/CHANGELOG.md compatibility notes and amended ADR 0108 myself. TDD held-out loop: implementer got per-layer happy-path tests (5 files), held out the full-chain integration test (shim->finalize_findings->normalize_finding->final review_result has no severity key -- the exact composition defect the gate caught) which validated GREEN after implementation, confirming the layers compose correctly. Mutation-teeth check in sandbox on the critical normalize_finding guard (mutated to always-clamp, confirmed the absent-key test goes RED while the present-invalid test stays green -- proving both behaviors independently tested). Full suite: 18318 passed, same 13 pre-existing environmental failures as before, zero regressions. Hit and resolved a real rebase conflict in generated docs/env-vars.md (4 sibling tickets landed to origin/main ahead of this one -- resolved by regenerating via the script, not hand-merging). Pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2462.","timestamp":1788156997072921685},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ticket 6's change 2462 got LLM-Review-1 with 1 blocking + 4 advisory findings, all legitimate: (1) docs/llm-framework.md's documented review_code() usage example unconditionally read f[\"severity\"], now updated to derive a label from decision when present; (2) docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md documented BLOCKING_SEVERITIES as a live operator-tunable en