summary (00-README), decide whether to re-run E3 on a quiet host, then final report to operator. Analysis dir also holds X1-X3 cross-model reviews.","timestamp":1788214826581976424},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"COMPLETION (2026-08-31): the overnight stability investigation is delivered. (1) Full corpus (22 docs) in .scratch/stability-analysis/ — start at 00-EXECUTIVE-SUMMARY.md; published report at https://claude.ai/code/artifact/29fbc8f9-3305-49ec-b9b0-6b851a69e9f5. (2) Bug horrendous-limpid-chamois (4eae-c207-7d7b-41f3) FIXED end-to-end by a dispatched subagent with no force: Gerrit change 2464 merged as 05be3a4dc6e4 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), ticket closed (close_class regression) with plan-review + completion-verifier attestations signed. Verified on origin/main: certification-time enqueue now gated on the same config pair the drain reads; suggest_duplicate_tickets=false in rebar.toml; RED-first regression test test_cert_with_drain_off_appends_no_queue_event. Observed gate wall-times: plan-review 2.2m, suite 16m37s, LLM-Review ~6m, Verified ~25m, completion-verifier 8.4m. Two hiccups resolved without force: a stale-store push-pending close refusal (cleared on next store push) and an MCP-server referencing-commit scan on a pre-merge clone (closed via local CLI per the gate's own guidance) — both are live examples of diagnosis M1/M2. Next steps for the operator are in 06-plan.md Part A (Day 0-2 items: scoreboard, close sweep, freeze submit-requirement, per-commit main CI).","timestamp":1788219379857490279},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Kickoff for story able-tidy-massasauga (e32d-6ea1-029a-435d). Read /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md + test-design.md, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/concurrency.md, and ADR 0106. Using a single fresh worktree /Users/joeoakhart/copilot-able-tid